(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["me-easy-2026-008"]={"v":1,"id":"me-easy-2026-008","title":"Basic Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","sourceTitle":"Basic Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME","branch":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING","code":"ME","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering","seriesId":"me-easy-2026","num":8,"category":"basic","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Mechanical Engineering"},"source":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Mechanical_Engineering/016_Basic Level Test-4 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 ME.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A book consists of 30 pages, 25 lines on each page and 35 characters on each line. If this content is written in another notebook consisting of 30 lines and 28 characters per line, then the required no. of pages will be how much percent greater than the previous pages?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4.16%"},{"key":"B","html":"5%"},{"key":"C","html":"6.66%"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/04addb0d3bb3f40625cf.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The rate of increase of the price of sugar is observed to be two percent more than the inflation rate expressed in percentage. The price of sugar on January 1, 2004 is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3f93f1c822cb38088a0b.png\" /> per kg. The inflation rates for the years 2004 and 2005 are expected to be 8% each. The expected price of sugar on January 1, 2006 would be :</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77d7d6f4de35cb57d249.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/59/59d0f66f3a96d9b1e359.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e1/e19a40f23f6c964d9427.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb03488fe23e7d541f62.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ca/ca1627876f8143b5585f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MSQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The following question is based on the diagram given below:<br />\n1. The rectangle represents government employees.<br />\n2. The triangle represents urban people.<br />\n3. The circle represents graduates.<br />\n4. The square represents clerks.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is true?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/39f936676d214453110f.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"All government employees are clerks."},{"key":"B","html":"Some government employees are graduates as well as clerks."},{"key":"C","html":"All government employees are graduates."},{"key":"D","html":"All clerks are government employees but not graduates."}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nThe above cases may be considered as under:<br />\nFor statement (a) to be true, the rectangle should lie inside the square. This is not true. Hence, (a) is false.<br />\nFor statement (b) to be true, there should be a region common to the rectangle, circle and the<br />\nsquare. Such a region is 6. Hence, (b) is true.<br />\nFurther, for statement (c) to be true, the rectangle should lie inside the circle. So, (c) is false.<br />\nFor statement (d) to be true, square should lie wholly inside the rectangle, with no region common<br />\nto the circle. This is not true. So, (d) is false.</p>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A square is inscribed in a circle and then another circle is inscribed in the square. Another square is inscribed in the circle. Finally, a circle is inscribed in the innermost square. Thus, there are 3 circles and 2 squares as shown in the figure. The radius of the outer-most circle is <em>R</em>.<br />\nWhat is the ratio of sum of circumferences of all the circles to the sum of perimeters of all the squares?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99f05d148937f1075001.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/06/064f1704381a9dc69b5a.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cc/cc205699d70906b08347.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f8/f838f32a6349d5df6548.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b414c5fc6319483f9c44.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/16f0af445cab04b90d31.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/3423416468bb89809804.png\" /></div>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which one of the following is the synonym of the word written in capital letter?<br />\nIRREVERENCE</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"disrespect"},{"key":"B","html":"cruelty"},{"key":"C","html":"unkindness"},{"key":"D","html":"invalidity"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nIrreverence means a lack of respect for the people or things which generally are taken seriously.</p>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Read the passage carefully and answer the following question.<br />\nChild psychology is certainly not a strong point with most Indian schools; why else would they inflict a double trauma on a student performing badly in the pre-boards by banning her from taking the board exams. Often with fatal results as evidenced by reports of student suicides in the run-up to the boards. Now the Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has stepped in and put the brakes on this discriminatory practice, ruling that no student can be barred from the Boards without prior clearance from the CBSE. This is good news for parents and students, many of whom have had to live with the threat of performance-linked debarment. While the school’s logic is that in order to attract talented students, they need to maintain their performance records at high levels. Chances are that a student faring poorly at the pre-boards will replicate at the boards is faulty. Chances are that the student will be spurred to work doubly hard. On the other hand, the threat of debarment, will almost certainly impact adversely on his/her performance. Of course, linking pre-boards to the boards is only one of the problems with our school system.<br />\nWhich is the good news for parents, according to the passage?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"School will take the responsibility of preparing students for the board."},{"key":"B","html":"School will provide study facilities to the poor student."},{"key":"C","html":"Schools will enforce discipline to ensure higher attendance of students."},{"key":"D","html":"No students can be barred from the Boards without prior clearance from the CBSE."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nFrom the above passage, it is apparent that the good news for parents is that no students can be<br />\nbarred from the Boards without prior clearance from the CBSE.</p>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The sum of n terms of two arithmetic series are in the ratio of  <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f8/f8f2757e9abe1dad3a4b.png\" /> Find the ratio of their 11<sup>th </sup>terms:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4 : 3"},{"key":"B","html":"5 : 4"},{"key":"C","html":"7 : 4"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d8133771b44128512c6a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A child is looking for his father. He went 90 m in the east before turning to his right. He went 20 m before turning to his right again to look for his father at his uncle’s place 30 m from this point. His father was not there. From there, he went 100 metres to his north before meeting his father in a street. How far did the son meet his father from the starting point?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"80 metres"},{"key":"B","html":"100 metres"},{"key":"C","html":"140 metres"},{"key":"D","html":"260 metres"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9bb3e91b476c8ca11db5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb3dac69d2949210c1d0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>400 student took the MOCK GATE exam in Lucknow. 60% of the boys and 80% of the girls cleared the cut-off in the examination. If the total percentage of students qualifying is 65%, then</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"100 girls appeared in the exam"},{"key":"B","html":"300 girls appeared in the exam"},{"key":"C","html":"200 boys appeared in the exam"},{"key":"D","html":"100 boys appeared in the exam"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/185579b3a050ada840a0.png\" /></div>\n</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For the mirror represented by a line MN, choose the correct mirror-image of the figure, from amongst the four alternatives (a), (b), (c) and (d) given along with it.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/09ad5c03ef2618092a9a.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b4aee0e1817ad6a5a822.png\" /></div>"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8a/8a63321459868b9c1645.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b3/b3ac8a66ef31c1bad8cd.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b6/b6c0a8d9c1926aec7498.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A Newtonian fluid having a specific gravity of 0.92 and a kinematic viscosity of 4 × 10<sup>–4</sup> m<sup>2</sup>/s flows past a fixed surface. The velocity profile near the surface is shown in the figure below. The magnitude of the shearing stress developed on the plate is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/df6c1930f6e59c2a990a.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/58/5851d1beca0772e73f28.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1be2200b8d45f0f850cc.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/05/05af028bda8d39426373.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/11/11fcfb20e69928f654b3.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/3928ee070507ae6659c7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A block of <em>m</em> kg moving with a velocity v strikes squarely the prismatic beam <em>AB</em> at its mid-point <em>C</em>. Simply supported at the ends as shown in the figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/39c27cd887c99e4e058f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Ignoring the change in potential energy. The maximum deflection of point <em>C</em> of the beam due to impact is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9f/9f604cf410a082ce4f7b.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d662e4597cddf2e0fae1.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/344a792c3678015748ff.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7f0612efae86797ecb47.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/25/2588f489d2fb5041ccd6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Two forces <em>P</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>P</em><sub>2</sub> are applied to a hook as shown in the figure. If the resultant of these two forces has a magnitude of 300 N and makes an angle of 30° with positive x-axis (anticlockwise direction), then the magnitudes (in N) of <em>P</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>P</em><sub>2</sub> will be</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/61/61066f40a75ea075f39f.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>P</em><sub>1</sub> = 155.3, <em>P</em><sub>2</sub> = 300"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>P</em><sub>1</sub> = 300, <em>P</em><sub>2</sub> = 155.3"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>P</em><sub>1</sub> = 150, <em>P</em><sub>2</sub> = 251.3"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>P</em><sub>1</sub> = 457.67, <em>P</em><sub>2</sub> = 153.5"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea9e581666ddea1233e0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1f1238e4ef6a982b3f45.png\" /></div>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which of the following Miller indices represents the plane shown below?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d0/d0aafc522034d6a5c115.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"(0 2 1)"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c3/c39b3eb189a902f5a902.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"(0 1 2)"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fb677dd9d808aaec1f15.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/32/32948307a14bad41d901.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>To punch a circular hole of 25 mm diameter from a 3 mm steel sheet whose shear strength is 290 MPa, the die and punch sizes respectively are</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"25 mm, 25.33 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"25.33 mm, 25 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"25 mm, 25.16 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"25.16 mm, 25 mm"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/82/82375693087c39ea27c8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":16,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The natural frequency of vibration of the system shown below is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2f/2f977670c938ce98cdc3.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The disc of mass 0.5 <em>M</em> is rigidly attached to massless rod and the point mass <em>M</em> is placed at the end <em>B</em>.</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c4/c4030ced4ff685b2cd1e.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6a/6a32e7bee6bddc3f55b9.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/76/769666c9544928982735.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8c/8c99d225b270f3b08818.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/161377c7c8e2c69654ae.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>What is the value of fatigue stress concentration factor due to a circular hole with Notch sensitivity of 0.875?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"3"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/25/25524262d726830ee7fc.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/991847610bf7827e5e51.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8e96f66b371607e2c353.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e238230d5bc6f015aae.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/15/15d9895bd845504dbdc7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A steam turbine receives steam at 20 bar and superheated by 88.6°C. The exhaust pressure is 0.07 bar and the expansion is isentropic. Refer the following data from steam table.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/05/05df39ae933f9c2c841c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>If the isentropic efficiency of turbine is 80%, then the actual work produced during expansion is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"738 kJ/kg"},{"key":"B","html":"730 kJ/kg"},{"key":"C","html":"678 kJ/kg"},{"key":"D","html":"573 kJ/kg"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/54b37dc8c5af106bdec2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>20 m<sup>3</sup> of air per minute at 27°C DBT and 70% RH is cooled to 20°C DBT while maintaining constant specific humidity. The saturation pressure at 27°C is 0.05125 bar. The heat removed from air is<br />\n[Take air pressure as 1 bar]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2.78 kJ/kg"},{"key":"B","html":"7.34 kJ/kg"},{"key":"C","html":"8.72 kJ/kg"},{"key":"D","html":"14.9 kJ/kg"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92e9243e4c3d811d8a31.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A project has the following activity durations (in weeks)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b9/b9825e3a6c78d9c002ab.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The critical path for the network is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 - 2 - 4 - 9 - 10"},{"key":"B","html":"1 - 3 - 4 - 9 - 10"},{"key":"C","html":"1 - 3 - 5 - 6 - 8 - 10"},{"key":"D","html":"1 - 3 - 5 - 7 - 8 - 10"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac06687af9d5e0c66bd8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following matrices have eigen values as 1 and –1?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/399d0f8268d3eae81d29.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ce/ce1ed440b673e00c2e0b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e64e9cbf9231ebfb0a0.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c4/c4b5886a9e48377e80a2.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)</p>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ed/ed2e47c3bec526ce3324.png\" /></div>\n</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":22,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>There are 3 fair coins and 1 false coin with tails on both sides. A coin is chosen at random and tossed 4 times. If tails occurs in all 4 times, then the probability that the false coin has been chosen for tossing is _______. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.8,0.87],"answerText":"0.84","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.84 (0.80 - 0.87)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/faa0dc31648dbb855d62.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/18e5a9a1f48a41bde416.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Each component with an area of 1055 mm<sup>2</sup> is to be blanked out of a stock strip of dimensions as shown below.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a7/a7f794970e5f21702712.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The percentage utilization of the stock is ______. [Round off to nearest integer]</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[67,67],"answerText":"67","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>67 (67 - 67)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/00a7423a45819d811d7e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A double riveted lap joint, having plate thickness of 20 mm, rivet hole diameter as 18 mm, rivet diameter of 17 mm, pitch of 50 mm. The tearing efficiency (in percentage) for the joint is_____. [Round off to nearest integer]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[64,64],"answerText":"64","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>64 (64 - 64)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fa/fa810616bd87a2017ce5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/51/515f46c4cf3699e565aa.png\" /></div>"},{"n":25,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A steel wire of diameter of 10 mm is formed into a coiled to a close coiled-helical spring having 10 active coils of mean diameter 75 mm. The spring has stiffness k. The percentage increase in stiffness if the same wire is recoiled into 15 active coils of mean diameter 50 mm is _____ %.<br />\n[Rounded off to nearest integer]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[125,125],"answerText":"125","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>125 (125 - 125)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/46a3d15bf4ce276d1941.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A copper slab of dimensions 0.4 m × 0.4 m and thickness 5 mm is initially at a uniform temperature of 250°C. Its surface are suddenly exposed to an ambient temperature of 30°C. The density, specific heat and thermal conductivity of the copper slab are 9000 kg/m3, 0.38 kJ/kgK and 370 W/mK respectively. The time required for the slab temperature to drop to 90° is _____ seconds. [Correct upto one decimal place]<br />\n[Take h = 90 W/m<sup>2</sup>K]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[115,135],"answerText":"123.4","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>123.4 (115 - 135)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0dc6ecb4c3497555b52f.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8d216107afe13b1cf67b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A roller of weight 800 N and radius 240 mm is pushed by force <em>P</em> (in N) over a step at <em>A</em> as shown in the figure. The magnitude of force <em>P</em> to just start the roller over the step is _____ N. (Rounded off to nearest integer)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/17dd37814d349d8140dd.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[656,660],"answerText":"658","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>658 (656 - 660)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/51/51e587b422710242ea4b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A crank and slotted lever quick return mechanism has a driving crank of length 8 cm and a slotted bar of length 19.5 cm. If the mechanism has a quick return ratio of 1.8, then the stroke length of the mechanism is _____ mm. [Rounded off to one decimal place]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[168.9,169.5],"answerText":"169.2","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>169.2 (168.9 - 169.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/67/67a65c6a062ca7748afb.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>In an orthogonal cutting operation a tool with a rake angle of 12° produces a chip with a chip thickness ratio of 0.25. The friction force on rake face is 1848 N and normal force on the rake face is 980 N. The error in shear angle by merchan’t relation compared to the actual shear angle is<br />\n_______ %. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[38.02,38.09],"answerText":"38.06","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>38.06 (38.02 - 38.09)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a2/a2baa7a67313a0345627.png\" /></div>"},{"n":30,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A bar of 30 mm diameter is subjected to a pull of 50 kN. The measured extension on gauge length of 200 mm is 0.08 mm and the change in diameter is 0.004 mm. The value of modulus of rigidity would be _____ GPa. [Correct upto to two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[65.5,67.5],"answerText":"66.48","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>66.48 (65.50 - 67.50)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/41/41542a53bb29c0b66d27.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A vertical glass tube of diameter 5 cm is sufficiently high, open at the top and containing a liquid, rotates about its vertical axis at 700 rpm. The depression of the lowest point of free liquid surface below the original horizontal surface when the liquid was at rest will be ______ cm. (Correct upto one decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8.3,8.9],"answerText":"8.6","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>8.6 (8.3 - 8.9)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7d1848658e8f6543d751.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":32,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>If the smoothing constant (α) is in an exponential smoothing forecast is 0.33, the number of periods of an equivalent simple moving average for the same response is ______. [Round off to nearest integer value]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5,5],"answerText":"5","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5 (5 - 5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ecd50a640e1773a6d9aa.png\" /></div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following is/are correct regarding Burgers vector in crystalline materials?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"For metallic materials, the magnitude of the Burgers Vector is equal to the interatomic spacing."},{"key":"B","html":"A Burger vector Changes direction and nature within a crystal."},{"key":"C","html":"For a mixed dislocation, the Burgers vector is parallel to the dislocation line."},{"key":"D","html":"For an edge dislocation, the Burgers vector is perpendicular to the dislocation Line."}],"answer":["A","B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)<br />\nThe nature of dislocation in crystal structure is defined by the relative orientation of dislocation Line and Burgers vector. For an edge dislocation, Burgers vector and dislocation line are perpendicular, whereas for a screw they are parallel they are neither parallel nor perpendicular for a mixed dislocation. Also, even though a dislocation changes direction and nature within a crystal, the Burgers vector will be the same at all points along its Line. For metallic materials, the Burgers vector for a dislocation will point in a closed-packed crystallographic direction and will be of magnitude equal to the interatomic spacing.</p>"},{"n":34,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>If variation between spectral blackbody emissive power and wavelength for selected temperature is plotted with wavelength as ordinate and spectral blackbody emissive power as abscissa, then<br />\nwhich of the following observation(s) drawn from the curve is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"At any specified temperature, emitted radiation increases with wavelength over the entire wavelength spectrum."},{"key":"B","html":"At any particular wavelength, amount of emitted radiation increases with increasing temperature."},{"key":"C","html":"As temperature increases, the peak spectral emissive power starts appearing at shorter wavelength."},{"key":"D","html":"The area under curve between spectral blackbody emissive power over entire wavelength spectrum at any specified temperature gives total blackbody emissive power."}],"answer":["B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C, D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b, c, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cf/cf791bbd3c5cd6129e66.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Two buses <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> are scheduled to arrive at a town central bus station at noon. The probability that bus <em>A</em> will be late is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/eb/ebb143c58ee429a1f68e.png\" /> The probability that bus <em>B</em> will be late is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e9f5f34979cfe7e374b.png\" /> The probability that the bus <em>B</em> is late given that bus <em>A</em> is late is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7ff451d30123db1dd186.png\" /> Then which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Probability that neither bus will be late on a particular day is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/dc/dc8d97e07a8010da6392.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"Probability that bus <em>A</em> is late given that bus <em>B</em> is late is  <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2f/2fb092e3c36573e00246.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"Probability that at least one bus is late is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/400dbab1aecb5f29ef02.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"Probability that at least one bus is in time is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/802dc4ecb6e5bfa81314.png\" />"}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/44fb3a85a2b0ccb11d5f.png\" /></div>\n</div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A homogeneous solid cylinder of radius 1 m and weight 1000 N with an initial clockwise angular velocity 30 rad/sec is placed in the corner formed by the floor and a vertical wall as shown in the figure. If the coefficient of Kinetic friction at <em>M</em> and <em>N</em> is 0.02 then the time required for cylinder to come to rest is [Take g = 10 m/s<sup>2</sup>]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f206ba83091ff0fbb7de.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"42.67 seconds"},{"key":"B","html":"35.25 seconds"},{"key":"C","html":"23.52 seconds"},{"key":"D","html":"73.53 seconds"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/780409b87f2ec3d9c3f0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":37,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Match <strong>List-I</strong> (Properties of molding sand) with <strong>List-II</strong> (Variation with water content) and select the correct answer using the codes given below the lists:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8c/8c6164681c8a56034de3.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91cf5d4b3868c83babc3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The piston cylinder arrangement contains gases at 3000°C and 60 bar. The gases expand through a volume ratio of 9 according to the law pv<sup>1.38</sup> = Constant. The surroundings are at 20°C, 1 bar. The work transfer of the gases per unit mass is<br />\n[Take, <em>R</em> = 0.26 kJ/kgK and <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/47/472b57a1e04dadb6c7f7.png\" /> = 0.82 kJ/kgK]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1420.15 kJ/kg"},{"key":"B","html":"1372.65 kJ/kg"},{"key":"C","html":"2921.11 kJ/kg"},{"key":"D","html":"1892.71 kJ/kg"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc2c4cb5f0eed5fca855.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A model of spillway is built to a scale of 1 : 36. If the model velocity and discharge are 1.25 m/s and 2.5 m<sup>3</sup>/s respectively, then corresponding prototype velocity and discharge are</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"7.5 m/s, 19440 m<sup>3</sup>/s"},{"key":"B","html":"17.5 m/s, 1944 m<sup>3</sup>/s"},{"key":"C","html":"6 m/s, 7776 m<sup>3</sup>/s"},{"key":"D","html":"19.44 m/s, 7.5 m<sup>3</sup>/s"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1d1ca5be4e61c4f74d68.png\" /></div>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A cavity of cross-section 20 cm × 20 cm and height 5 cm is to be filled completely in 5 sec by using top gating system. The cross-sectional area of the gate is 3 cm<sup>2</sup>, and the height of pouring basin is 2.5 cm. The height of sprue required to achieve the desired filling time is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"90.61 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"81.29 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"65.61 mm"},{"key":"D","html":"73.16 mm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec8fb87a87ff749c5d12.png\" /></div>"},{"n":41,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A bimetallic cylindrical bar of cross-sectional area 1 m2 is made by bonding steel (<em>E</em> = 210 GPa) and aluminium (<em>E</em> = 70 GPa) as shown in figure. To maintain tensile axial strain of magnitude 10<sup>–6</sup> in steel bar, the magnitude of the required force P along indicated direction is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/91e0c8ce82a55ac3054b.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"70 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"140 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"210 kN"},{"key":"D","html":"280 kN"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d5229c68f7444875dc27.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>For a planer linkage consisting of only lower-pairs with 17 revolute joints and 6 number of loops.<br />\nThe degree of freedom of the linkage is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"0"},{"key":"D","html":"-1"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/87/873c1afcd381469b7f6c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In an absorption refrigeration system, the heating, cooling and refrigeration take place at 127°C, 27°C and –23°C respectively. Some changes in heating and refrigeration temperatures causes an 11.2% decrease in the theoretical COP. If the heating temperature is increased to 177°C, the refrigeration temperature is decreased to</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"–42.3°C"},{"key":"B","html":"–28.9°C"},{"key":"C","html":"–38.5°C"},{"key":"D","html":"–36.4°C"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0e495cc0ccf5e794646a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b87a022ef74092b2bfba.png\" /></div>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A short shoe drum brake is shown in figure:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/236358d2ee260f1a6933.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>A force of 1 kN is applied on the lever. The coefficient of friction is 0.5. The magnitude of braking torque applied is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"705.882 Nm"},{"key":"B","html":"400 Nm"},{"key":"C","html":"352.94 Nm"},{"key":"D","html":"200 Nm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b92ab9a93dc1b5c4b50.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8ea677bdaa347e604e2c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Balaji corporation currently practices the following system for the procurement of an item.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0c/0cde0a541a06273e7850.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The loss to the company for not practising a scientific inventory policy (EOQ) is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1cd70c7aa81f60ed2b5d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/78bcdc87a358ce9cd4e8.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9db88d575c83619cf541.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3f97b2a26aee86fc4d5f.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ca/cac6dc2fbd420cf207c5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1c/1c164f7d2d90d728e38e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A four cylinder engine running at 4200 rpm, using natural gas, develops a brake power of 70 kW. The engine details are : Air gas ratio 9 : 1, calorific value of fuel 40 MJ/m<sup>3</sup>, compression ratio 10 : 1, volumetric efficiency 90%, mechanical efficiency 80% and the total volume of the engine is 2.4 litres. The indicated thermal efficiency of the engine is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"39%"},{"key":"B","html":"35%"},{"key":"C","html":"23%"},{"key":"D","html":"29%"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f7/f7236ca824544b03d809.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Let a function <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/93/93ff453de4461b35d7f7.png\" />Then which of the following statements is not true regarding <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>)?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Discontinuous at <em>x</em> = 0"},{"key":"B","html":"Discontinuous at <em>x</em> = 1"},{"key":"C","html":"Not differentiable at <em>x</em> = 0"},{"key":"D","html":"Not differentiable at <em>x</em> = 1"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/72/72509ef052040af45352.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If <em>A<sub>n</sub></em> is the area bounded by <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5a06ec9870dbf2be38c.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/37832f0d860b5e72c39f.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e9/e9b64dc3af5536ca826f.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/563099117a89b6bdff87.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd5d5ee793b08a09bcfe.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f3b3ddf301e5cf81b29e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/29/29ea2e3119e800a4e470.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>For the state of stress as shown in figure,</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/16/162611b0ab1d020ef3f9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The orientation of the plane with maximum shear stress with respect to the x-axis will be _____<br />\ndegrees. (Correct upto one decimal place)</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"-22.5° and 67.5°"},{"key":"B","html":"22.5° and -67.5°"},{"key":"C","html":"22.5° and 67.5°"},{"key":"D","html":"-22.5° and -67.5°"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/142283427e699f4e311b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n</div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A tapered circular rod of diameter varying from 60 mm to 40 mm is connected to another circular tapered rod of diameter varying from 40 mm to 70 mm as shown in figure below. Both bars are of same material having modulus of elasticity of 2 × 10<sup>5</sup> MPa. When subjected to a load of 100 kN, the vertical deflection of point <em>A</em> is ________ mm. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6b37ecb5c1a904fe61f4.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.49,1.54],"answerText":"1.52","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.52 (1.49 - 1.54)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/641b20858282029c4ea0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For the given configuration the angular velocity of the connecting rod in rad/min is [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1e/1e095c5de37d8d8ed781.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[400,410],"answerText":"403.98","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>403.98 (400 - 410)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b3/b37c0f1397181642c966.png\" /></div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A centrifugal pump delivers water against a net head of 20 m at a speed of 1000 rpm. The vanes are curved backward at 30° to the periphery. The impeller radius is 10 cm and the impeller outlet width is 5 cm. If the manometric effeciency is 95%, then the discharge of the pump is _______ m<sup>3</sup>/s.<br />\n[Correct upto three decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.155,0.175],"answerText":"0.168","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.168 (0.155 - 0.175)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/1857083d4c0997dda005.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The difference in forecast for the fourth period according to weighted moving average of 3 periods and simple moving average of 3 periods is _____. [Round off to two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/9156c48eea2684eb4702.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.3,2.4],"answerText":"2.33","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.33 (2.30 - 2.40)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/8966460fd56e790f5601.png\" /></div>"},{"n":54,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Water flows out from a tank of cross-sectional area 1000 mm<sup>2</sup> through a small orifice of area 10 mm<sup>2</sup>, located at y = 0. Initially water is at level y = 1 m as shown in figure.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d4/d4373a2e1a06a1138a18.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Considering the acceleration due to gravity as 10 m/s<sup>2</sup>, the time taken to reach water level at y = 0.4 m is _____ seconds. (Correct upto two decimal places)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[15,17],"answerText":"16.44","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>16.44 (15 - 17)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/79/79069e23248dc271a5d0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bc/bca554f1db2cd75f02d1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The net radiation from the surfaces of two parallel plates maintained at temperatures, T<sub>1</sub> and T<sub>2</sub><br />\nis to be reduced by 79 times.  The number of radiation screens to be placed between the<br />\ntwo surfaces to achieve this reduction in heat exchange, assuming the emissivity of the screens as<br />\n0.05 and that of the surfaces as 0.8 is ____ ( rounded of to the nearest integer )</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3,3],"answerText":"3","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>3 (3- 3)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cd/cdeb31d3384a345ef70d.png\" /></div>\n</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A simple brayton cycle operates between the temperature limits of 27°C and 1127°C. The ratio of maximum efficiency to the optimum efficiency of the cycle is _____. [Round off to two decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1.45,1.47],"answerText":"1.46","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>1.46 (1.45 - 1.47)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f6a8865b642d9ad07113.png\" /></div>"},{"n":57,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An aluminium rod of diameter 26 mm is to be extruded through a die with a semi-die cone angle of 4° and the coefficient of friction is 0.12. The maximum possible reduction in cross-sectional area during extrusion is ______ %. [Correct upto one decimal place]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[24.3,25.2],"answerText":"24.8","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>24.8 (24.3 - 25.2)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77f16e55bc3d6eac44a9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/93/933fc0f5d8ef442d6762.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The natural frequency of vibration of system shown in the figure below is _______ Hz. [Correct upto two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6c63ef1c1658a71c9cf2.png\" /></div>\n</div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.1,0.14],"answerText":"0.12","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.12 (0.10 - 0.14)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bf/bf09080b86e838d4cd4e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>An insulated, vertical piston cylinder device initially contain 10 kg of water, 6 kg of which is in the vapour phase. The mass of piston is such that it maintains a constant pressure of 200 kPa inside the cylinder. Now steam at 0.5 MPa and 360°C is allowed to enter the cylinder from a supply line until all the liquid in the cylinder has vaporized. The mass of steam that has entered is<br />\n________ kg. [Round off to two decimal places]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3c/3cca1f955b4cfc683068.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[18.05,18.45],"answerText":"18.24","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>18.24 (18.05 - 18.45)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/67/67a5a2a478adf1398dfc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dd/dd6435a9ea9922bfd4d7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":60,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A flow of 0.5 kg/s of exhaust gas at 427°C from a gas turbine is used to preheat the incomming air which is at ambient temperature of 27°C. It is desired to cool the exhaust to 400 K, It is estimated that the overall heat transfer coefficient is 10 W/m<sup>2</sup>K. The heat capacity of the exhaust gases is same as that of air i.e. 1.2kJ/kgK and the mass flow rate of air is equal to that of the exhaust gas.<br />\nIf the heat exchanger is designed as a counterflow device, the required heat transfer area is _______ m<sup>2</sup>. [Rounded off to nearest integer]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[180,180],"answerText":"180","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>180 (180 - 180)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/35532eaaf9ec8669b32b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>It is required to weld low carbon steel plate by the manual metal arc welding process using a<br />\nlinear VI characteristic D.C. power source.<br />\nThe following data are available:<br />\nOpen circuit voltages of power source = 60 V<br />\nShort circuit current = 130 A<br />\nArc length, L = 4 mm<br />\nTransverse speed of welding = 15 cm/min<br />\nVoltage is given as V = 20 + 1.5L, where L being arc length in mm.<br />\nEfficiency of heat input = 84%</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The heat input to the workpiece is nearly 1.6 kW."},{"key":"B","html":"The heat input to the workpiece is nearly 3.6 kW."},{"key":"C","html":"The voltage and current of the source required are 73.67 V and 26 A respectively."},{"key":"D","html":"The voltage and current of the source required are 26 V and 73.67 A respectively."}],"answer":["A","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/20/202a8ff3d403610577d0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following is/are the main differences between reversed carnot cycle operating on perfect gas and wet vapour?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Work of isentropic compression is equal to work of isentropic expansion in case of perfect gas, but for wet vapour region the work of isentropic compression is more than work of isentropic expansion."},{"key":"B","html":"Work of isentropic compression is more than work of isentropic expansion, but for wet vapour region, the work of isentropic compression is equal to isentropic expansion."},{"key":"C","html":"Work during isothermal condensation and isothermal evaporation is zero for wet vapour region but for perfect gas there is work transfer during isothermal compression and expansion."},{"key":"D","html":"Work during isothermal condensation and isothermal evaporation is not zero, but for perfect gas work during isothermal compression and expansion is zero."}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, c)<br />\nThe main differences between reversed carnot cycle operating on perfect gas and wet vapour are:<br />\n1. Work of isentropic compression is equal to work of isentropic expansion in case of perfect<br />\ngas, and thus algebraic work for these two processes is zero. But for wet vapour region the<br />\nwork of isentropic compression is more than work of isentropic expansion. In fact, the net<br />\nwork of the cycle is difference between the two.<br />\n2. Work during isothermal condensation = 0. And work during isothermal evaporation = 0, for<br />\nwet vapour region. But the difference of heat transfer during condensation and evaporation<br />\nis the net work of the cycle. For perfect gas there is both heat transfer and work transfer<br />\nduring isothermal compression and isothermal expansion. Algebraic sum of heat transfer is<br />\nequal to algebraic sum of work transfer during isothermal processes for perfect gas.</p>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The solution of the differential equation y′′′ − 8y′′ = 0, where <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/53/53e0c8123f60288a931a.png\" /> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7c/7cfabc58ea3a1e5e7a62.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e0/e04b69b6d9e3af18d50b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8ed81be23a00dbd945ca.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c3/c3bf50ccddedbb901392.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A unit normal to the level surface x<sup>2</sup> – y<sup>2</sup> + z = 2 at (1, –1, 2) is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e2a1d03ad9181984570d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6ce797319e085228e746.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/716ba27c2511de9e9f31.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fd/fd32da01aafb5a54b956.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • MECHANICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>If Mean = (3 Median – Mode)<em>A</em>, then the value ‘<em>A</em>’ is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/88bdcdfb712c812a5f93.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/48/482fc344aa3f382e3dd2.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2ddffb63be26d284e1a4.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":36,"MSQ":7,"NAT":22},"withoutKey":0}};
